001700*REMARKS.
001800**************************************************************
001900*D  C C O D E C H K      CODE CHECK SUBPROGRAM               *
002000*D                                                           *
002100*D  THIS SUBPROGRAM DETERMINES IF AN MSTORERM "CORP-CODE"    *
002200*D  IS A "CORPORATE" CODE OR A "PLANT" CODE.  THE CALLING    *
002300*D  PROGRAM PASSES BOTH THE CODE AND THE PLANT NUMBER, AND   *
002400*D  THIS SUBPROGRAM RETURNS A ONE BYTE FLAG TO IDENTIFY THE  *
002500*D  CODE TYPE.                                               *
002600*                                                            *
002700*   WHETHER A CODE IS A "CORPORATE" CODE OR A "PLANT" CODE   *
002800*   IS FUNCTION OF BOTH THE PLANT AND THE ACTUAL FORMAT OF   *
002900*   THE CODE ITSELF.   IF A PLANT IS DEFINED AS A            *
003000*   "STAND ALONE" PLANT IN THE COPYLIB.DB MEMBER PLANTS THEN *
003100*   ALL OF THAT PLANT'S MSTORERM CODES ARE CONSIDERED        *
003200*   "PLANT" CODES.   FOR ALL OTHER PLANTS, THE FORMAT OF THE *
003300*   CODE IDENTIFIES THE TYPE OF CODE IT IS.   THE CURRENT    *
003400*   RULE ESTABLISHED BY CME IS THAT A "PLANT" CODE WILL      *
003500*   CONTAIN AT LEAST ONE ALPHABETIC CHARACTER (A THRU Z) IN  *
003600*   POSITIONS 5, 6, AND 7 OF THE SEVEN CHARACTER CODE.       *
003700*   ALTERNATIVELY, A "CORPORATE" CODE WILL CONTAIN ONLY      *
003800*   NUMERIC CHARACTERS AND/OR SPACES IN POSITIONS 5, 6, AND  *
003900*   7.                                                       *
004000*                                                            *
004100**************************************************************
